ESP32 Framework Core
Overview
ESP32 Framework Core is a modular, production-oriented embedded framework for building scalable IoT, automation, and device-control systems on ESP32 hardware.
It provides a structured architecture for:
* Parameter registry and persistent configuration
* WiFi management
* MQTT integration
* Telnet access
* REST/API services
* Command processing
* Logging and diagnostics
* Health monitoring
* Watchdog protection
* Time synchronization (NTP + timezone)
* Modular subsystem expansion
The framework is designed for:
* Industrial controllers
* Smart home systems
* Remote monitoring devices
* Sensor hubs
* Custom firmware platforms

Key Features
Core System
* Centralized ParamManager for all configuration
* ParamStorageManager with flash persistence
* Registry checksum validation for schema mismatch detection
* Automatic factory reset on registry structure changes
* Event bus architecture
* Modular startup and lifecycle management

Connectivity
WiFi Module
* STA/AP support
* Auto reconnect
* Signal diagnostics
* IP/network monitoring
MQTT Module
* Secure broker authentication
* Parameter publishing by flags/tags
* Health metrics publishing
* Remote parameter control
* Device status topics
Telnet Module
* Remote CLI management
* Live diagnostics
* Configuration access
API Module
* HTTP API endpoints
* External integrations

Diagnostics & Reliability
Logger Module
* Human-readable timestamped logs
* Log levels:
o DEBUG
o INFO
o WARNING
o ERROR
o CRITICAL
* Serial logging
* MQTT/syslog ready architecture
* Dynamic profiling support
TimeManager
* NTP synchronization
* Configurable timezone support
* Periodic resync
* Human-readable datetime for logs
Watchdog Module
* Runtime failure tracking
* Stability monitoring
* Automatic health reports

