Command Interface
Core Commands
* help
* status
* factory_reset
* reboot
* list
Parameter Commands
* get <param>
* set <param> <value>
* info <param>
* reset <param>
Extended Diagnostics
* Schema ID
* Registry checksum
* WiFi status
* MQTT status
* Heap health
* Profiling state
* Current timezone
* NTP sync status

Configuration Safety
The framework protects against firmware/registry mismatches:
On boot:
* Validates schema ID
* Validates registry checksum
* Detects added/removed/reordered parameters
* Automatically restores factory defaults if mismatch detected
* Optional auto reboot after recovery
This prevents corrupted settings after firmware upgrades.

Logging Format
[2026-05-10 14:32:18][INFO][SYSTEM] Framework boot started
[2026-05-10 14:32:19][INFO][WiFi] Connected successfully
[2026-05-10 14:32:22][WARNING][MQTT] Broker reconnect attempt failed

Performance Profiling
Optional runtime profiling tracks module loop duration:
[PROFILE][WiFiManager] 4 ms
[PROFILE][MQTTModule] 7 ms
[PROFILE][Storage] 2 ms
Useful for:
* Bottleneck detection
* Watchdog tuning
* Optimization
* Production diagnostics

Build Requirements
Hardware
* ESP32 DevKit / ESP32-WROOM / compatible ESP32 boards
Software
* Arduino IDE or PlatformIO
* ESP32 Board Package
* PubSubClient
* WiFi library
* Preferences / NVS

Installation
Clone repository
git clone https://github.com/YOUUSERNAME/esp32-framework-core.git
Open project
* Arduino IDE
* Select ESP32 board
* Configure BuildConfig.h
* Upload firmware

